-- title:
--   Equal raw classes give the same Γ₀(M') moduli point
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, let $\ell', M', q$ be natural numbers with $M' \neq 0$, and let $h\ell$, $hM$ be the two variable-change compatibilities: for every commutative $A$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$ and every variable change $C$, a level-$\ell'$ datum $D$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.IsLevelPStructure`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelP.html#L104) for $W$ has its transport `D.variableChange C` satisfying it for $C \bullet W$; and for all $p,k$ and $h \in T[X]$, `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` implies `IsGamma0PowAt (C \bullet W) p k` of `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be group laws over $A$ and $\mathcal{T}$ a level transport for $\mathcal{G}$ at $q$, and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field that is an $A$-algebra with $M' \neq 0$ in $\kappa$. Let $x, x'$ be raw data over $\kappa$ for the rigid datum `rigidDataPow A ℓ' M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯` — each a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant together with level data for it — and assume $x$ and $x'$ have the same class in the quotient `Pt κ`. Let $g$ be a $\kappa$-point of `x.curve` and $g'$ a $\kappa$-point of `x'.curve`, each of exact additive order $M'$, and each cut out by the $\Gamma_0$-component of its level datum: for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every $n$ and every affine nonsingular point $(x_1,y_1)$ with $n \cdot g = (x_1,y_1)$ of exact order $p^{v_p(M')}$, the abscissa $x_1$ is a root of the $p$-th polynomial of the first component of `x.level` (likewise for $g'$ and `x'.level`). Then the two $\Gamma_0(M')$-pairs $(\,$`x.curve`$, g)$ and $(\,$`x'.curve`$, g')$, elliptic by the unit-discriminant hypotheses, have equal classes in `ModuliPoint M' κ`, i.e. they agree modulo the relation generated by the existence of a variable change matching the curves and carrying one generator to a multiple of the other by an integer coprime to $M'$.
--
--   This is the passage from the rigid full-level moduli problem with prime-power $\Gamma_0(M')$, level-$\ell'$ and Drinfeld-$\Gamma(q)$ data down to the coarse $\Gamma_0(M')$ moduli set: raw data in one class of the rigid quotient, equipped with generators cut out by their $\Gamma_0$-tuples, determine one and the same $\Gamma_0(M')$ moduli point. It is the converse direction of the corresponding alignment statement, and is used in the Tate-curve analysis of the full-level problem and in the identification of the cyclic-quotient $j$-invariant along $A$-algebra maps.
